/-!
# Closed orbits of a real flow, their least periods, iterates and multiplicities

Let `ϕ` be a continuous flow by `ℝ` on a `T₁` space. The times `t` with `ϕ t x = x` form a closed
subgroup `Flow.periods ϕ x` of `ℝ`, which is the same for all points on one orbit. Unless `x` is a
rest point, this subgroup is not all of `ℝ`, hence it is discrete and generated by the **least
period** `Flow.leastPeriod ϕ x`, the least positive return time
(`Flow.periods_eq_zmultiples_leastPeriod`). The least period is `0` exactly at rest points and at
points that never return.

A *periodic trajectory* (`Flow.PeriodicTrajectory`) is a point which is not a rest point together
with a positive return time `τ`; it is the parametrized loop `t ↦ ϕ t x` on `[0, τ]`. Flowing the
base point rotates the loop, and a **closed orbit** (`Flow.ClosedOrbit`) is a periodic trajectory
up to rotation. A closed orbit is determined by its image and its period (`Flow.ClosedOrbit.ext`).
Its period is a positive integer multiple of the least period of its points; this integer is its
**multiplicity** `Flow.ClosedOrbit.multiplicity`, the covering degree of the closed orbit over the
underlying simple loop. The multiplicity is not the return time.

The `k`-fold iterate `Flow.ClosedOrbit.iterate` runs `k` times around the same loop: it has the
same image and least period, `k` times the period and `k` times the multiplicity. A closed orbit
is primitive (`Flow.ClosedOrbit.IsPrimitive`) when its period is the least period, and every
closed orbit is the `m`-fold iterate of a unique primitive closed orbit, where `m` is its
multiplicity. Hence closed orbits correspond to pairs of a primitive closed orbit and a positive
integer (`Flow.ClosedOrbit.equivPrimitiveProdPNat`). This is the indexing of the orbit sums
`∑_γ ε(γ) / p(γ) · e^[γ]` in the dynamical zeta function of a flow: a sum over all closed orbits
`γ`, with `p(γ)` the multiplicity, is a sum over the primitive closed orbits and all their
iterates.

## Main definitions

* `Flow.periods ϕ x`: the subgroup of times `t` with `ϕ t x = x`.
* `Flow.leastPeriod ϕ x`: the infimum of the positive periods of `x`.
* `Flow.PeriodicTrajectory ϕ`: a point which is not a rest point with a positive return time; the
  flow acts on these by rotation.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit ϕ`: periodic trajectories up to rotation.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.period`, `Flow.ClosedOrbit.leastPeriod`, `Flow.ClosedOrbit.support`: the
  return time, the least period and the image of a closed orbit.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.multiplicity`: the positive integer `period / leastPeriod`.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.iterate γ k`: the `k`-fold iterate of `γ`.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.primitive γ`: the primitive closed orbit underlying `γ`.

## Main results

* `Flow.periods_eq_zmultiples_leastPeriod`: off rest points, the periods are the integer
  multiples of the least period.
* `Flow.leastPeriod_pos_iff`: the least period is positive exactly at periodic points which are
  not rest points.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.ext`: a closed orbit is determined by its image and its period.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.multiplicity_mul_leastPeriod`: the period is the multiplicity times the least
  period.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.primitive_iterate_multiplicity`: every closed orbit is the iterate of its
  primitive closed orbit by its multiplicity.
* `Flow.ClosedOrbit.equivPrimitiveProdPNat`: closed orbits correspond to primitive closed orbits
  with a positive number of iterations.

## References

* M. Hutchings and Y.-J. Lee, *Circle-valued Morse theory and Reidemeister torsion*,
  Geom. Topol. 3 (1999), 369–396, Section 2.
* D. Fried, *Lefschetz formulas for flows*, Contemp. Math. 58, Part III (1987), 19–69.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Set

namespace Flow

variable {α : Type*} [TopologicalSpace α] (ϕ : Flow ℝ α) {x : α} {s t : ℝ}

/-! ### Periods and the least period of a point -/

/-- The periods of `x` under the flow `ϕ`: the times `t` with `ϕ t x = x`. This is the stabilizer
of `x` for the action of `ℝ` by the flow. -/
def periods (x : α) : AddSubgroup ℝ := @AddAction.stabilizer ℝ α _ ϕ.toAddAction x

@[simp]
theorem mem_periods : t ∈ ϕ.periods x ↔ ϕ t x = x :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem apply_comm (s t : ℝ) (x : α) : ϕ s (ϕ t x) = ϕ t (ϕ s x) := by
  rw [← map_add, add_comm, map_add]

/-- All points of an orbit have the same periods. -/
@[simp]
theorem periods_apply (s : ℝ) (x : α) : ϕ.periods (ϕ s x) = ϕ.periods x := by
  ext t
  rw [mem_periods, mem_periods, apply_comm]
  exact (ϕ.toHomeomorph s).injective.eq_iff

/-- All points of an orbit have the same orbit. -/
@[simp]
theorem orbit_apply (s : ℝ) (x : α) : orbit ϕ (ϕ s x) = orbit ϕ x :=
  @AddAction.orbit_vadd ℝ α _ ϕ.toAddAction s x

theorem periods_eq_of_mem_orbit {x y : α} (h : y ∈ orbit ϕ x) : ϕ.periods y = ϕ.periods x := by
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := (mem_orbit_iff ϕ).1 h
  exact ϕ.periods_apply s x

theorem isClosed_periods [T1Space α] (x : α) : IsClosed (ϕ.periods x : Set ℝ) :=
  isClosed_singleton.preimage (ϕ.continuous continuous_id continuous_const)

/-- The least period of `x`: the infimum of the positive times `t` with `ϕ t x = x`. It is `0` at
rest points and at points which never return (`Flow.leastPeriod_pos_iff`). -/
def leastPeriod (x : α) : ℝ :=
  sInf {t | t ∈ ϕ.periods x ∧ 0 < t}

@[simp]
theorem leastPeriod_apply (s : ℝ) (x : α) : ϕ.leastPeriod (ϕ s x) = ϕ.leastPeriod x := by
  simp [leastPeriod]

theorem leastPeriod_eq_of_mem_orbit {x y : α} (h : y ∈ orbit ϕ x) :
    ϕ.leastPeriod y = ϕ.leastPeriod x := by
  simp [leastPeriod, ϕ.periods_eq_of_mem_orbit h]

theorem leastPeriod_nonneg (x : α) : 0 ≤ ϕ.leastPeriod x :=
  Real.sInf_nonneg fun _ ht ↦ ht.2.le

theorem leastPeriod_le (ht : ϕ t x = x) (ht₀ : 0 < t) : ϕ.leastPeriod x ≤ t :=
  csInf_le ⟨0, fun _ hs ↦ hs.2.le⟩ ⟨ht, ht₀⟩

theorem leastPeriod_eq_zero_of_forall_apply_eq (hx : ∀ t, ϕ t x = x) : ϕ.leastPeriod x = 0 := by
  simp only [leastPeriod, mem_periods, hx, true_and]
  exact csInf_Ioi

/-- Off rest points, the least positive period exists and generates all periods. -/
theorem periods_eq_zmultiples_leastPeriod [T1Space α] (hx : ∃ t, ϕ t x ≠ x) :
    ϕ.periods x = AddSubgroup.zmultiples (ϕ.leastPeriod x) := by
  by_cases hbot : ϕ.periods x = ⊥
  · have : {t | t ∈ ϕ.periods x ∧ 0 < t} = ∅ := by
      ext t
      simp only [hbot, AddSubgroup.mem_bot, mem_empty_iff_false, iff_false]
      rintro ⟨rfl, h⟩
      exact h.false
    unfold leastPeriod
    rw [this, Real.sInf_empty, AddSubgroup.zmultiples_zero_eq_bot, hbot]
  -- A closed subgroup of `ℝ` without least positive element is dense, hence everything.
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ : ∃ a, IsLeast {t | t ∈ ϕ.periods x ∧ 0 < t} a := by
    by_contra h
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hx
    have hdense := AddSubgroup.dense_of_no_min _ hbot h
    have : t ∈ (ϕ.periods x : Set ℝ) := by
      rw [← (ϕ.isClosed_periods x).closure_eq, hdense.closure_eq]
      exact mem_univ t
    exact ht this
  unfold leastPeriod
  rw [ha.csInf_eq, AddSubgroup.zmultiples_eq_of_isLeast_mem_and_pos ha]

theorem apply_eq_self_iff_exists_zsmul [T1Space α] (hx : ∃ t, ϕ t x ≠ x) :
    ϕ t x = x ↔ ∃ n : ℤ, n • ϕ.leastPeriod x = t := by
  rw [← mem_periods, ϕ.periods_eq_zmultiples_leastPeriod hx, AddSubgroup.mem_zmultiples_iff]

@[simp]
theorem apply_leastPeriod [T1Space α] (x : α) : ϕ (ϕ.leastPeriod x) x = x := by
  by_cases hx : ∃ t, ϕ t x ≠ x
  · have : ϕ.leastPeriod x ∈ ϕ.periods x := by
      rw [ϕ.periods_eq_zmultiples_leastPeriod hx]
      exact AddSubgroup.mem_zmultiples _
    exact this
  · simp only [not_exists, not_not] at hx
    exact hx _

/-- The least period is positive exactly at periodic points which are not rest points. -/
theorem leastPeriod_pos_iff [T1Space α] :
    0 < ϕ.leastPeriod x ↔ (∃ t, ϕ t x ≠ x) ∧ ∃ t ≠ 0, ϕ t x = x := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨?_, _, h.ne', ϕ.apply_leastPeriod x⟩, fun ⟨hx, t, ht₀, ht⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  · by_contra hx
    simp only [not_exists, not_not] at hx
    exact h.ne' (ϕ.leastPeriod_eq_zero_of_forall_apply_eq hx)
  obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := (ϕ.apply_eq_self_iff_exists_zsmul hx).1 ht
  refine (ϕ.leastPeriod_nonneg x).lt_of_ne fun h ↦ ht₀ ?_
  rw [← h, smul_zero]

/-! ### Periodic trajectories and closed orbits -/

/-- A periodic trajectory of `ϕ`: a point `point` which is not a rest point, together with a
positive return time `period`. It is the loop `t ↦ ϕ t point` on `[0, period]`; its rotations are
the trajectories obtained by flowing the base point. -/
@[ext]
structure PeriodicTrajectory where
  /-- The base point of the trajectory. -/
  point : α
  /-- The return time of the trajectory. -/
  period : ℝ
  period_pos : 0 < period
  apply_period : ϕ period point = point
  exists_apply_ne : ∃ t, ϕ t point ≠ point

namespace PeriodicTrajectory

variable {ϕ}

/-- The flow acts on periodic trajectories by rotation: `s +ᵥ γ` has base point `ϕ s γ.point`
and the same period. -/
instance : AddAction ℝ (PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) where
  vadd s γ :=
    { point := ϕ s γ.point
      period := γ.period
      period_pos := γ.period_pos
      apply_period := by rw [ϕ.apply_comm, γ.apply_period]
      exists_apply_ne := by
        simpa [← mem_periods, ϕ.periods_apply] using γ.exists_apply_ne }
  zero_vadd γ := by ext <;> simp [HVAdd.hVAdd]
  add_vadd s t γ := by ext <;> simp [HVAdd.hVAdd, map_add]

@[simp]
theorem point_vadd (s : ℝ) (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : (s +ᵥ γ).point = ϕ s γ.point :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem period_vadd (s : ℝ) (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : (s +ᵥ γ).period = γ.period :=
  (rfl)

/-- The `k`-fold iterate of a periodic trajectory: the same base point with `k` times the return
time. -/
def iterate (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ where
  point := γ.point
  period := k * γ.period
  period_pos := mul_pos (by exact_mod_cast k.pos) γ.period_pos
  apply_period := by
    have h : (k : ℕ) • γ.period ∈ ϕ.periods γ.point := nsmul_mem γ.apply_period _
    rwa [nsmul_eq_mul, mem_periods] at h
  exists_apply_ne := γ.exists_apply_ne

@[simp]
theorem point_iterate (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : (γ.iterate k).point = γ.point :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem period_iterate (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) (k : ℕ+) :
    (γ.iterate k).period = k * γ.period :=
  (rfl)

theorem vadd_iterate (s : ℝ) (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) (k : ℕ+) :
    s +ᵥ γ.iterate k = (s +ᵥ γ).iterate k :=
  (rfl)

theorem leastPeriod_pos [T1Space α] (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : 0 < ϕ.leastPeriod γ.point :=
  ϕ.leastPeriod_pos_iff.2 ⟨γ.exists_apply_ne, _, γ.period_pos.ne', γ.apply_period⟩

/-- The primitive periodic trajectory with the same base point: its return time is the least
period. -/
def primitive [T1Space α] (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ where
  point := γ.point
  period := ϕ.leastPeriod γ.point
  period_pos := γ.leastPeriod_pos
  apply_period := ϕ.apply_leastPeriod _
  exists_apply_ne := γ.exists_apply_ne

@[simp]
theorem point_primitive [T1Space α] (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : γ.primitive.point = γ.point :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem period_primitive [T1Space α] (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) :
    γ.primitive.period = ϕ.leastPeriod γ.point :=
  (rfl)

theorem vadd_primitive [T1Space α] (s : ℝ) (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) :
    s +ᵥ γ.primitive = (s +ᵥ γ).primitive := by
  ext <;> simp

end PeriodicTrajectory

/-- A closed orbit of `ϕ`: a periodic trajectory up to rotation. A closed orbit may be multiply
covered; its multiplicity is `Flow.ClosedOrbit.multiplicity`. -/
abbrev ClosedOrbit := AddAction.orbitRel.Quotient ℝ (PeriodicTrajectory ϕ)

namespace ClosedOrbit

variable {ϕ}

/-- The closed orbit of a periodic trajectory. -/
def mk (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : ClosedOrbit ϕ :=
  Quotient.mk'' γ

theorem mk_surjective : Function.Surjective (mk : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ → ClosedOrbit ϕ) :=
  Quotient.mk''_surjective

@[elab_as_elim]
theorem ind {p : ClosedOrbit ϕ → Prop} (h : ∀ γ, p (mk γ)) (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : p γ :=
  Quotient.ind' h γ

theorem mk_eq_mk_iff {γ γ' : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ} : mk γ = mk γ' ↔ ∃ s : ℝ, s +ᵥ γ' = γ :=
  Quotient.eq''.trans AddAction.orbitRel_apply

@[simp]
theorem mk_vadd (s : ℝ) (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : mk (s +ᵥ γ) = mk γ :=
  mk_eq_mk_iff.2 ⟨s, rfl⟩

/-- The common return time of the periodic trajectories of a closed orbit. -/
def period (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : ℝ :=
  Quotient.liftOn' γ PeriodicTrajectory.period fun γ γ' h ↦ by
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := AddAction.orbitRel_apply.1 h
    rfl

/-- The common least period of the points of a closed orbit. -/
def leastPeriod (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : ℝ :=
  Quotient.liftOn' γ (fun γ ↦ ϕ.leastPeriod γ.point) fun γ γ' h ↦ by
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := AddAction.orbitRel_apply.1 h
    simp

/-- The image of a closed orbit: the orbit of any of its points. -/
def support (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : Set α :=
  Quotient.liftOn' γ (fun γ ↦ orbit ϕ γ.point) fun γ γ' h ↦ by
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := AddAction.orbitRel_apply.1 h
    exact ϕ.orbit_apply s γ'.point

@[simp]
theorem period_mk (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : (mk γ).period = γ.period :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem leastPeriod_mk (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : (mk γ).leastPeriod = ϕ.leastPeriod γ.point :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem support_mk (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : (mk γ).support = orbit ϕ γ.point :=
  (rfl)

theorem period_pos (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : 0 < γ.period :=
  γ.ind fun γ ↦ γ.period_pos

theorem leastPeriod_pos [T1Space α] (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : 0 < γ.leastPeriod :=
  γ.ind fun γ ↦ γ.leastPeriod_pos

theorem leastPeriod_le_period (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.leastPeriod ≤ γ.period :=
  γ.ind fun γ ↦ ϕ.leastPeriod_le γ.apply_period γ.period_pos

/-- A closed orbit is determined by its image and its period. -/
@[ext]
theorem ext {γ γ' : ClosedOrbit ϕ} (hs : γ.support = γ'.support) (hp : γ.period = γ'.period) :
    γ = γ' := by
  induction γ using ind with | h γ => ?_
  induction γ' using ind with | h γ' => ?_
  simp only [support_mk, period_mk] at hs hp
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (mem_orbit_iff ϕ).1 (hs ▸ mem_orbit_self ϕ γ.point)
  exact mk_eq_mk_iff.2 ⟨s, PeriodicTrajectory.ext hs hp.symm⟩

/-- The `k`-fold iterate of a closed orbit, running `k` times around it. -/
def iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : ClosedOrbit ϕ :=
  Quotient.liftOn' γ (fun γ ↦ mk (γ.iterate k)) fun γ γ' h ↦ by
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := AddAction.orbitRel_apply.1 h
    rw [← PeriodicTrajectory.vadd_iterate]
    exact mk_vadd _ _

@[simp]
theorem iterate_mk (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : (mk γ).iterate k = mk (γ.iterate k) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem period_iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : (γ.iterate k).period = k * γ.period :=
  γ.ind fun _ ↦ (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem leastPeriod_iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k : ℕ+) :
    (γ.iterate k).leastPeriod = γ.leastPeriod :=
  γ.ind fun _ ↦ (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem support_iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : (γ.iterate k).support = γ.support :=
  γ.ind fun _ ↦ (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem iterate_one (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.iterate 1 = γ := by
  ext <;> simp

theorem iterate_iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k l : ℕ+) :
    (γ.iterate k).iterate l = γ.iterate (l * k) := by
  ext <;> simp [mul_assoc]

/-- A closed orbit is primitive if its period is the least period of its points, that is, if it
runs once around a simple loop. -/
def IsPrimitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : Prop :=
  γ.period = γ.leastPeriod

theorem isPrimitive_iff {γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ} : γ.IsPrimitive ↔ γ.period = γ.leastPeriod :=
  Iff.rfl

section T1Space

variable [T1Space α]

/-- The multiplicity of a closed orbit: the positive integer `period / leastPeriod`, the covering
degree of the closed orbit over the underlying simple loop. -/
def multiplicity (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : ℕ+ :=
  ⟨⌊γ.period / γ.leastPeriod⌋₊, Nat.floor_pos.2 <|
    (one_le_div γ.leastPeriod_pos).2 γ.leastPeriod_le_period⟩

/-- The period of a closed orbit is its multiplicity times its least period. -/
theorem multiplicity_mul_leastPeriod (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) :
    (γ.multiplicity : ℝ) * γ.leastPeriod = γ.period := by
  induction γ using ind with | h γ => ?_
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (ϕ.apply_eq_self_iff_exists_zsmul γ.exists_apply_ne).1 γ.apply_period
  have hT := γ.leastPeriod_pos
  rw [zsmul_eq_mul] at hn
  have hn₀ : (0 : ℝ) < n := (pos_iff_pos_of_mul_pos (hn ▸ γ.period_pos)).2 hT
  lift n to ℕ using (by exact_mod_cast hn₀.le)
  simp only [multiplicity, PNat.mk_coe, period_mk, leastPeriod_mk, ← hn, Int.cast_natCast]
  rw [mul_div_cancel_right₀ _ hT.ne', Nat.floor_natCast]

theorem multiplicity_eq_iff {γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ} {k : ℕ+} :
    γ.multiplicity = k ↔ (k : ℝ) * γ.leastPeriod = γ.period := by
  rw [← γ.multiplicity_mul_leastPeriod, mul_left_inj' γ.leastPeriod_pos.ne', Nat.cast_inj,
    PNat.coe_inj, eq_comm]

@[simp]
theorem multiplicity_iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k : ℕ+) :
    (γ.iterate k).multiplicity = k * γ.multiplicity := by
  rw [multiplicity_eq_iff, period_iterate, leastPeriod_iterate, ← multiplicity_mul_leastPeriod]
  push_cast
  ring

theorem isPrimitive_iff_multiplicity_eq_one {γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ} :
    γ.IsPrimitive ↔ γ.multiplicity = 1 := by
  rw [multiplicity_eq_iff, PNat.one_coe, Nat.cast_one, one_mul, isPrimitive_iff, eq_comm]

/-- The primitive closed orbit underlying a closed orbit: the same loop, run once. -/
def primitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : ClosedOrbit ϕ :=
  Quotient.liftOn' γ (fun γ ↦ mk γ.primitive) fun γ γ' h ↦ by
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := AddAction.orbitRel_apply.1 h
    rw [← PeriodicTrajectory.vadd_primitive]
    exact mk_vadd _ _

@[simp]
theorem primitive_mk (γ : PeriodicTrajectory ϕ) : (mk γ).primitive = mk γ.primitive :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem period_primitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.primitive.period = γ.leastPeriod :=
  γ.ind fun _ ↦ (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem leastPeriod_primitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.primitive.leastPeriod = γ.leastPeriod :=
  γ.ind fun _ ↦ (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem support_primitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.primitive.support = γ.support :=
  γ.ind fun _ ↦ (rfl)

theorem isPrimitive_primitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.primitive.IsPrimitive := by
  simp [isPrimitive_iff]

theorem IsPrimitive.primitive_eq {γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ} (hγ : γ.IsPrimitive) : γ.primitive = γ := by
  ext
  · simp
  · simpa using (isPrimitive_iff.1 hγ).symm

@[simp]
theorem primitive_iterate (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) (k : ℕ+) : (γ.iterate k).primitive = γ.primitive := by
  ext <;> simp

@[simp]
theorem multiplicity_primitive (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) : γ.primitive.multiplicity = 1 :=
  isPrimitive_iff_multiplicity_eq_one.1 γ.isPrimitive_primitive

/-- Every closed orbit is the iterate of its primitive closed orbit by its multiplicity. -/
@[simp]
theorem primitive_iterate_multiplicity (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) :
    γ.primitive.iterate γ.multiplicity = γ := by
  ext
  · simp
  · simp [multiplicity_mul_leastPeriod]

/-- Closed orbits correspond to primitive closed orbits together with a positive number of
iterations, by taking the iterate. -/
def equivPrimitiveProdPNat : ClosedOrbit ϕ ≃ {γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ // γ.IsPrimitive} × ℕ+ where
  toFun γ := (⟨γ.primitive, γ.isPrimitive_primitive⟩, γ.multiplicity)
  invFun p := p.1.1.iterate p.2
  left_inv γ := γ.primitive_iterate_multiplicity
  right_inv := fun ⟨⟨γ, hγ⟩, k⟩ ↦ by
    refine Prod.ext (Subtype.ext ?_) ?_
    · simp [hγ.primitive_eq]
    · simp [isPrimitive_iff_multiplicity_eq_one.1 hγ]

@[simp]
theorem equivPrimitiveProdPNat_apply (γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ) :
    equivPrimitiveProdPNat γ = (⟨γ.primitive, γ.isPrimitive_primitive⟩, γ.multiplicity) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem equivPrimitiveProdPNat_symm_apply (p : {γ : ClosedOrbit ϕ // γ.IsPrimitive} × ℕ+) :
    equivPrimitiveProdPNat.symm p = p.1.1.iterate p.2 :=
  (rfl)

end T1Space

end ClosedOrbit

end Flow
